  "result": "I fixed the duplicate-delivery bug in `src/lib/event-bus.ts`. I haven't run the test suite; per the project rules I didn't run any git or install commands.\n\nThe cause was in `subscribe()`. Every subscribe copies the handler set, and the unsubscribe closure deleted from the copy it had captured. Once a later subscribe on the same event type had replaced that set, the delete hit a stale copy and the handler stayed live. Each detach/re-attach cycle therefore added another copy of the activity, search, usage and webhook handlers. Notifications are attached once at module load and never detached, which is why they were never duplicated.\n\nThe unsubscribe now looks up the live set for that event type when it runs. Detaching removes the handler, and calling it again is a no-op. `emit()` already snapshots the set before iterating, so the copy-on-write behaviour is unchanged. `registerEventHandlers()` already returns early when handlers are attached, so registering again without detaching remains a no-op.",
